# Git commits: Conventional Commits

Create a commit only when the user explicitly asks. Follow the existing git safety protocol (no force push, no amend unless allowed, no `--no-verify`, HEREDOC for the message).

## Format

```
<type>(<optional-scope>): <description>

<optional body>
```

- `type` is required; `scope` is optional (module/area: `ui`, `engine`, `config`, `tests`)
- Description: English, imperative mood, lowercase after the colon, no trailing period, ~50 characters, max 72
- Body (optional): wrap at 72 chars; explain **why**, not what. Use a blank line after the subject
- Breaking change: `type(scope)!: description` and/or a footer `BREAKING CHANGE: ...`

## Types

| type | when |
|------|------|
| `feat` | new user-facing capability |
| `fix` | bug fix |
| `docs` | README or comments only |
| `style` | formatting, no logic change |
| `refactor` | restructure without behavior change |
| `perf` | performance |
| `test` | add or update tests |
| `build` | deps, packaging, `requirements*.txt` |
| `ci` | CI config |
| `chore` | tooling, gitignore, misc non-code |

Pick **one** type that matches the primary intent. Prefer `feat`/`fix` over `chore` when behavior changes.

## Examples

```
# ❌ BAD
Update test suite to enhance coverage for precision handling.
Fixed the bug.
feat: Added FP8 support.

# ✅ GOOD
feat(engine): add fp8 precision as the default
fix(ui): show current precision in the status bar
test: cover env loading and precision error paths
docs: document cu130 install for RTX 50xx
```
